                <pb facs="0416" n="320" sameAs="frus:frus1898/pg320"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Day to Mr. White.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1898-02-07"><hi rendition="#italic">February 7,
                        1898</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Closing part of fruit decree authorizes imperial chancellor to make exceptions to
                    the prohibition and regulate precautionary measures. Does this enable merchants
                    to be heard in their own behalf, and thus obtain relief in favorable cases and
                    admission of goods where not infected?</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Day</hi>, <hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Acting.</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
